This color-role example leaves other Material roles at their defaults. A published enterprise theme must also define the roles it uses for errors, containers, typography, shapes, and component states. Product code reads `MaterialTheme` roles or approved semantic extensions instead of copying these literals.

### iOS · adaptive named assets

Generate the named color assets below with light/dark variants in the owning asset catalog. Supply that catalog's bundle explicitly when it is outside the application bundle.

`Core/Design/EnterpriseTheme.swift`

```swift
import Foundation
import SwiftUI

struct EnterpriseTheme: ViewModifier {
    let resourceBundle: Bundle

    func body(content: Content) -> some View {
        content
            .tint(Color("foundation.primary", bundle: resourceBundle))
            .foregroundStyle(Color("foundation.textPrimary", bundle: resourceBundle))
            .background(Color("foundation.background", bundle: resourceBundle))
    }
}

extension View {
    func enterpriseTheme(resourceBundle: Bundle = .main) -> some View {
        modifier(EnterpriseTheme(resourceBundle: resourceBundle))
    }
